 "findings": {
  "F1_ff_hold_is_the_output_budget": "All 128 FF hold violators below -45 ps are output ports (pval/prow/pseg/pnseg/ppos/perr/pv/busy/fault): set_output_delay -min -0.56 ns makes the port require data stable until 585 ps after the ideal edge, while the block launches at its own clock latency (311.6 ps FF, 555.9 ps SS) + ~58 ps. The same pair of budgets is checked at SS for setup (out max -0.193 ns: arrive by 906 ps). Any output path with block latency + delay D_SS at SS and k*D_SS at FF needs k*D_SS >= 585 and D_SS <= 906, i.e. k >= 0.646; measured k = 0.56 (clock 311.6/555.9) and 0.565 (pval[15] path 370.0/655.3). The I/O budget is therefore infeasible for every RTL; FF output hold cannot close by any latency L. -0.56 ns equals the SS clock insertion of a sibling q element (555.9 ps); a corner-consistent FF budget would be its FF insertion (~-0.32 ns). Changing it is a constraint decision for the owner and is NOT applied here.",
  "F2_internal_ff_hold": "Internal FF hold WNS -44.2 ps (b_xs_q0 -> r_xs_q0, pa_sh -> p1_sh, delay lines, i2 -> p0_xq), capture-minus-launch clock +19..+60 ps: ordinary CTS skew on short paths; ORFS repaired hold at the WC (SS) corner only (driver WC hold -11.2 ps). Not a gated-vs-free tree mismatch: 293 of 299 launch and 299 of 299 capture clocks pass the ICG.",
  "F3_icg_skew_signature_in_setup": "The gated/free latency mismatch is real but bites SETUP: the ICG sits at the root (CLK latency 69 ps SS), the gated tree adds ~480 ps, and CTS balances the free-clock registers with 11 BUFx24 delay buffers (548.7 ps). rst_q (free) -> AND4/INV -> ICG ENA therefore has 833 - 480 - 60 - 73 (ICG setup) ps: -81.8 ps at SS.",
  "F4_yosys_merged_the_per_macro_copies": "Yosys 0.68 opt_merge merges flip-flops with identical inputs even when the reg carries (* keep *) / dont_touch (reproduced on a 2-register test in the ORFS image). The routed netlist holds u_e.g_mac[0].g_l3.u_l{0,1}.p0_xq only (256 each, none in g_mac[1]), r_i2_bk only in g_mac[1], fwd5/fwd6 only in g_mac[0]: one register drives both macro halves across the 510 um die (macros at x=5 and x=380). Worst SS setup r_i2_bk -> p0_wq -236 ps (147 + 114 ps wire segments), cap0 -> p0_we -166 ps, r_i2_t -> p0_wq -106 ps, fwd5 -> fadd -67 ps (64 of 299 top paths cross halves). The QPIPE per-macro copies never existed in silicon.",
  "F5_walker": "w_c -> wA/wB/w_lu_r/w_h/w_j -69..-111 ps at SS (single-cycle walker recurrence, ~850 ps data path, capture-minus-launch -35 ps). Was -18..-61 ps at R_cap1 CTS; not pipelinable without halving issue rate.",
  "F6_reset_recovery": "rst_q -> fadd y / pair y / tree y RESETN recovery -52 ps at SS (one synchroniser drives every asynchronous reset)."
 }
}